\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The folders made from where you call \texttt  {focex-agent.py} (here \texttt  {~/calc}, with \texttt  {PROJECT_NAME: Si}). \texttt  {focex-agent.py} writes the project folder, \texttt  {01_relax/}, \texttt  {run_workflow.sh} and \texttt  {resubmit_failed.sh} at once; every other step folder is made when its task runs, in the order of the numbers except \texttt  {06_dfpt}, which runs right after \texttt  {02_scf} (the numbering of VASP-Flow). Each VASP folder is an ordinary VASP folder. In mode \texttt  {extract_only} there are no \texttt  {01}--\texttt  {03} folders: \texttt  {04_supercells/} holds your data, rotated into the FOCEX frame, and \texttt  {05_focex/} the fit.}}{16}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:project-tree}{{1}{16}{The folders made from where you call \cmd {focex-agent.py} (here \cmd {~/calc}, with \cmd {PROJECT_NAME: Si}). \cmd {focex-agent.py} writes the project folder, \cmd {01_relax/}, \cmd {run_workflow.sh} and \cmd {resubmit_failed.sh} at once; every other step folder is made when its task runs, in the order of the numbers except \cmd {06_dfpt}, which runs right after \cmd {02_scf} (the numbering of VASP-Flow). Each VASP folder is an ordinary VASP folder. In mode \cmd {extract_only} there are no \cmd {01}--\cmd {03} folders: \cmd {04_supercells/} holds your data, rotated into the FOCEX frame, and \cmd {05_focex/} the fit}{figure.1}{}}
